{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nGuidelines:\n- Do not infer missing logic\n- Do not create domain-specific content\n- Only manipulate the text the user describes\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `utils.py`.\n\nAdd a reset method to the Calculator class that sets result to 0 and returns it"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"utils.py\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "class Calculator:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.result = 0\n    \n    def add(self, value):\n        self.result += value\n        return self.result\n", "tool_call_id": "call_44c4b0e93aae"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"utils.py\", \"contents\": \"class Calculator:\\n    def __init__(self):\\n        self.result = 0\\n    \\n    def add(self, value):\\n        self.result += value\\n        return self.result\\n    \\n    def reset(self):\\n        self.result = 0\\n        return self.result\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_55355e067880"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nGuidelines:\n- Do not infer missing logic\n- Do not create domain-specific content\n- Only manipulate the text the user describes\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `main.py`.\n\nAdd a reset method to the Calculator class that sets result to 0 and returns it"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"main.py\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "class Calculator:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.result = 0\n    \n    def add(self, value):\n        self.result += value\n        return self.result\n", "tool_call_id": "call_9cab161598e0"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"main.py\", \"contents\": \"class Calculator:\\n    def __init__(self):\\n        self.result = 0\\n    \\n    def add(self, value):\\n        self.result += value\\n        return self.result\\n    \\n    def reset(self):\\n        self.result = 0\\n        return self.result\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_9b47dd42be73"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nGuidelines:\n- Do not infer missing logic\n- Do not create domain-specific content\n- Only manipulate the text the user describes\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `handler.go`.\n\nAdd an 'Age' field of type int to the User struct"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"handler.go\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "package main\n\ntype User struct {\n\tName  string\n\tEmail string\n}\n\nfunc (u *User) String() string {\n\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"User: %s\", u.Name)\n}\n", "tool_call_id": "call_ae382cb27226"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"handler.go\", \"contents\": \"package main\\n\\ntype User struct {\\n\\tName  string\\n\\tEmail string\\n\\tAge   int\\n}\\n\\nfunc (u *User) String() string {\\n\\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\\\"User: %s\\\", u.Name)\\n}\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_be9878c66093"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nGuidelines:\n- Do not infer missing logic\n- Do not create domain-specific content\n- Only manipulate the text the user describes\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `data.json`.\n\nUpdate the version field to '2.0.0'"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"data.json\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{\n  \"name\": \"MyApp\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"author\": \"John Doe\",\n  \"license\": \"MIT\"\n}\n", "tool_call_id": "call_0573533ff057"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"data.json\", \"contents\": \"{\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"MyApp\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"2.0.0\\\",\\n  \\\"author\\\": \\\"John Doe\\\",\\n  \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\"\\n}\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_52f56ffeb3e7"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
