{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nGuidelines:\n- Do not infer missing logic\n- Do not create domain-specific content\n- Only manipulate the text the user describes\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `client.go`.\n\nAdd the 'time' package to imports and print the current time in main"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"client.go\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "package main\n\nimport \"fmt\"\n\nfunc main() {\n\tfmt.Println(\"Hello\")\n}\n", "tool_call_id": "call_60c3606861e3"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"client.go\", \"contents\": \"package main\\n\\nimport (\\n\\t\\\"fmt\\\"\\n\\t\\\"time\\\"\\n)\\n\\nfunc main() {\\n\\tfmt.Println(\\\"Hello\\\")\\n\\tfmt.Println(\\\"Time:\\\", time.Now())\\n}\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_218edbf94c89"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
