{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nGuidelines:\n- Do not infer missing logic\n- Do not create domain-specific content\n- Only manipulate the text the user describes\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `k8s.yaml`.\n\nSet cache to true, add analytics: true under features, and set debug to false"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"k8s.yaml\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "app:\n  features:\n    auth: true\n    cache: false\n  settings:\n    debug: true\n", "tool_call_id": "call_d8ea3bbe33e5"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"k8s.yaml\", \"contents\": \"app:\\n  features:\\n    auth: true\\n    cache: true\\n    analytics: true\\n  settings:\\n    debug: false\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_c5afe3016ab7"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
