{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nGuidelines:\n- Do not infer missing logic\n- Do not create domain-specific content\n- Only manipulate the text the user describes\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `config.json`.\n\nAdd 'package3' to dependencies array and 'dev2' to devDependencies array"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"config.json\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "{\n  \"dependencies\": [\n    \"package1\",\n    \"package2\"\n  ],\n  \"devDependencies\": [\n    \"dev1\"\n  ]\n}\n", "tool_call_id": "call_c54c872199a4"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"config.json\", \"contents\": \"{\\n  \\\"dependencies\\\": [\\n    \\\"package1\\\",\\n    \\\"package2\\\",\\n    \\\"package3\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"devDependencies\\\": [\\n    \\\"dev1\\\",\\n    \\\"dev2\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\\n\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_49d61b4756cf"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
